{"id": 73, "ts": 1780422833.4516675, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to keep Candidate\u202fC as my provisional choice.\u202fSarah\u2019s notes confirm that C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d which directly addresses the crew\u2011cooperation criterion and suggests he can foster a constructive cockpit environment\u2014an essential factor for long\u2011haul operations.\u202fAt the same time, the same source flags \u201cdifficulty communicating ideas,\u201d which is a legitimate concern for professional communication, but I view it as less detrimental than the interpersonal hostility reported for Candidate\u202fB (who \u201cmakes nasty remarks about his colleagues\u201d) and the hot\u2011tempered behavior noted for Candidate\u202fD.\u202fC also demonstrates decisive, rapid decision\u2011making, stays calm in crises, and understands complex technology, all of which are high\u2011priority safety competencies.\u202fWhile his egocentric attitude and limited appetite for further education are noted, these do not outweigh his strong cooperation and decision\u2011quality strengths relative to the alternatives.\nTherefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC, pending any further evidence on how his communication difficulty might be mitigated in practice."}
