{"id": 80, "ts": 1780422870.0997722, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fB has been noted to \u201cmake nasty remarks about his colleagues,\u201d which raises a serious red flag for professional communication and crew cooperation\u2014both non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance operations. Combined with the earlier concerns that B can be grumpy and uncooperative, his interpersonal profile now appears weaker than I initially assumed.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC is described as 100\u202f% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, and creates a positive atmosphere with his crew. While C does have difficulty communicating ideas and is seen as egocentric, those issues have not been reported as overtly hostile or disruptive, and his reliability and decision quality directly address the core safety\u2011critical criteria.\nGiven the new evidence on B\u2019s communication shortcomings, I am moving my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fC**, as his strengths in reliability and decision quality outweigh the comparatively milder communication concerns."}
